s can basically tell you  the most uh commonly searched for terms  or how frequently people are searching  for these terms  uh in comparison to other terms my point  with this  is to say most people who play video  games because again there are millions  upon millions upon millions of gamers  may have heard of naughty dog may have  seen the splash screen but that's as far  as it goes they don't talk to their  friends about these studios they don't  know who neil druckmann is they don't  know about  leaks they don't know about any of the  controversies that exist  on the internet that feel like when  you're part of the online  games community feel like the biggest  news in the entire world so let's  have a look if i search for last of us  two  metacritic so metacritic little bump  right there  still pales in comparison to the video  game um  of course there are people who could be  searching for the last of us part two  and finding metacritic on the first page  etc you know this data is not  one-to-one um but there isn't really any  way to prove it so it's just  a visual representation you could pick a  million holes in that i would never use  it in an  actual journalistic piece of any kind it  doesn't work that way  just trying to find a way to illustrate  my point to put a visual to my  point but basically i've seen a lot of  people say um  things along the lines of everyone hates  the last of us part two everyone hates  this game  uh if it wins any awards these awards  are rigged if you look at the user score  on metacritic versus the review score  you can see the public hates this game  the real gamers hate this game  and i don't think that's true at all i  think that majority of the gamers of the  four million people who bought that game  in june alone don't even know what  metacritic is have never looked at  metacritic before in their lives  it is a very specific small group  of people who are part of the video game  internet culture who ever look at  metacriti